  "result": "`Date.prototype.toString` is implemented in `prototype_to_string.rs` and passes 14 of 16 runs under `built-ins/Date/prototype/toString/`. The two failures are `negative-year.js` (sloppy and strict), which expects `\"-0001\"` and gets `\"-000001\"`. That comes from `year_string` in `support/date.rs`, which pads negative years with `{:06}` where the spec's DateString uses `ToZeroPaddedDecimalString(abs(yv), 4)`. That file is outside my ticket scope, so I left it alone and did not reimplement DateString in my file.\n\n`this_time_value` already throws a TypeError for non-Date receivers, so RequireInternalSlot steps 1\u20132 are covered. `cargo clippy -p kahvi-builtins` is clean.\n\nBLOCKED: `support/date.rs` `year_string` must pad negative years with `{:04}` instead of `{:06}` (spec DateString: `-` plus `ToZeroPaddedDecimalString(abs(yv), 4)`); this needs an architect-owned fix or a scope exception for that file.",
